    "report": "The conversation hid contact details again after a cancellation because the paid-stay lookup excluded cancelled bookings. I removed that exclusion and committed the fix on `main` as `1d86ebf`. Nothing was pushed.\n\n**Cause:** `PostgresBookingQueries.hasPaidStay` (`src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts`) had `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'` in its SQL. Once the stay was cancelled, Messaging got `false` and masked the host's messages again. ADR 55 says a cancelled or refunded paid stay keeps lifting the hold. Cancellation and refund change the separate refund status, not the payment's `paid`/`declared` status, so removing the clause is enough.\n\n**Change:**\n- Removed the `cancelled` filter from `hasPaidStay`. Nothing else in the query or the conversation view changed.\n- Added an e2e case in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`: a paid stay that the traveller then cancels still shows the host's contact details in full.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The new case fails without the fix and passes with it.\n- The full e2e run (114 suites, 608 tests) passes, and typecheck and lint are clean.\n- `yarn test:e2e` ignored my path filter and ran the whole suite, which took about three minutes. I didn't start a server, so port 4471 wasn't used.\n\n**Choices and unclear points:**\n- The request didn't say whether the old behaviour was intended. I went with ADR 55, which is explicit that cancelled and refunded paid stays keep the lift.\n- I did not check whether the payment status changes anywhere else on cancellation. The code I read suggests it doesn't.",
